A thread that joins a ring is not linked from the newest thread before it.
A signal or a switch would never reach it, and the ring would not close;
a queue is a ring linked both ways.

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -33,3 +33,3 @@ static void ring_push(paddr_t *head, struct thread *t)
         t->queue_prev = oldest->queue_prev;
-        newest->queue_next = self;
+        (void)newest;
         oldest->queue_prev = self;
